tau init - write a commented starter ~/.config/tau/config.json

Usage:
  tau init [--force] [--stdout] [--dry-run] [--provider <name>] [--json]

Options:
      --force            Overwrite an existing config file
      --stdout           Print the starter config without writing it
                         (mutex with --json/--dry-run)
      --dry-run          Preview the exact files and config the scaffold
                         would write (files[] + JSONC body in the result
                         object); change nothing (mutex with --stdout)
      --provider <name>  Scaffold for a specific provider
      --json             Pin the stable schema-checked result object
                         (schema/tau-init.schema.json)

On success a getting-started checklist (next steps: `tau setup --client`,
`tau doctor`, `tau explain --list`) is printed to stderr — including under
--dry-run; stdout stays a pure JSON result object or the JSONC scaffold
under --stdout.

Examples:
  tau init
  tau init --provider openai
  tau init --stdout
  tau init --dry-run
  tau init --force
